"""Reduced cortical cells from the Hagen et al. (2016) hybrid-LFP morphologies (Cereb. Cortex 26:4461,
doi:10.1093/cercor/bhw237; files ``morphologies/stretched/*.hoc`` of hybridLFPy).

Each morphology is reduced to depth profiles relative to its soma: in 10 um bins counted from the
soma's surface, upward (toward the pia) and downward, the membrane area (um^2) and the mean over the
bin of the Rall sum ``sum(d^1.5)`` over the branches crossing each depth plane. The soma keeps its
path length and its area-equivalent diameter. Profiles were generated by script from these files
(SHA-256):
#   L23E_oi24rpy1.hoc  c488448a4094c6c42a7c0cbefce81eb3c851267cdf87a064fcb7c6943c8fd6c8
#   L23I_oi38lbc1.hoc  5412db138f3e048f0a2d3710c988a9b5dbb8f76f1a1ddf0dd43faabe69b3a4de
#   L4E_53rpy1.hoc  ff4adcfedab9a0afee21259d0cf3c65294daed090da43c91e65ec5fd22601312
#   L4E_j7_L4stellate.hoc  6aa6a14b8d237eaa4efeed833788d3304d23cab0f1c573bdfcdf01393ded3cd4
#   L4I_oi26rbc1.hoc  c578cf3a95bd12eae4a839503476e9504b4b28daf66603ea6789dab4085a3271
#   L5E_j4a.hoc  6b1059bee6b30822a5c94613deffc6dcef2f08824f4c8edca91ff2679aec7267
#   L5E_oi15rpy4.hoc  7a219bb66432d070d21f922ee424b58b0ee142ae922e7a0c6db7bc8785dbbd43
#   L5I_oi15rbc1.hoc  926aa1371c433c5bd01e78301abaa67e211f6d96409960ce48e8b3ac2cbfcfc8
#   L6E_51-2a.CNG.hoc  9755095a8728b38c1f965727a1555c3f566cc0917fbacbf9063fa62c92e5df43
#   L6E_oi15rpy4.hoc  7b1cf24822209d645567e11b90aaffa1d6679dbdc2a2e22864e49409d154bb4b
#   L6I_oi15rbc1.hoc  926aa1371c433c5bd01e78301abaa67e211f6d96409960ce48e8b3ac2cbfcfc8

The stretched cells sit in Hagen's cat V1 column with layer boundaries ``SOURCE_BOUNDS_UM`` (pia,
L1|L2/3, L2/3|L4, L4|L5, L5|L6, white matter) and somata at their layer's midpoint; from there the
apical tufts of ``L23E_oi24rpy1``, ``L4E_53rpy1``, ``L5E_j4a``, ``L5E_oi15rpy4`` and ``L6E_oi15rpy4`` end
within one bin of the pia, and ``L6E_51-2a.CNG`` ends in L2/3. :func:`hagen2016_cell`
places a population's cell in a target column by mapping depth piecewise-linearly from these
boundaries to the target's (linear extrapolation beyond them), so a tuft that reaches L1 in the source
reaches L1 in the target. A population with several morphologies averages their profiles with equal
weights. These are reduced, derived cells: the profile keeps the membrane area per depth and the
axial-equivalent diameter; the branching is dropped.
"""

